### Remove a newly created config when registration fails

**Severity:** `medium`

CreateProfile creates the config before registering it in settings.json. If registration throws, it returns false but leaves the config behind, so the directory scan discovers a profile whose creation was reported as failed. Roll back the newly created config when registration throws, then rethrow so the existing error handler still reports failure. The existing deletion helper logs a rollback failure.

```suggestion
                try
                {
                    JsonObject root = (ReadSettingsRoot() as JsonObject) ?? CreateDefaultSettingsRoot();
                    JsonObject properties = EnsureObject(root, "properties");
                    AddToConfigurationList(properties, profile);
                    WriteSettingsRoot(root);
                    return true;
                }
                catch
                {
                    TryDeleteFile(target);
                    throw;
                }
```

### Create the default profile before selecting it

**Severity:** `medium`

GetProfiles always offers default, but SetActiveProfile rejects it when default.json has not yet been created. A fresh installation can therefore offer a default profile that cannot be selected. Call the existing missing-only default initializer before checking the config file. The subsequent existence check still rejects a failed creation.

```suggestion
                if (profile.Equals(DefaultProfile, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
                {
                    EnsureDefaultProfileExists();
                }

                if (!File.Exists(ConfigPath(profile)))
```
